This skill's subject is consulting current third-party documentation and
implementation code, so its cases cannot be measured offline. Evaluated
offline, the skill correctly refuses to implement without research and
produces nothing, losing to a baseline that guesses from memory.

They cannot be measured online either, on the models this repository pins.
The 5.6 family cannot use the web-search tool: it answers

    403 Forbidden: Selected provider is forbidden

and falls back to memory or to a direct API call, often without saying so.
`gpt-5.5` searches normally, checked with the same question from the same
empty directory, so this is the model rather than the account.

Presence of this file makes scripts/shuhari_staged_targets.sh skip this
skill's behavior cases and say why. The cases stay in evals.json rather
than being deleted: they are correct, and deleting them would mean nobody
notices when the constraint lifts. Delete this file to put them back under
the gate — which is also the check for whether the constraint has lifted,
since the cases will simply pass once the model can search.
